37. Pattern: ticket-led comp growth

Condition:

comparable sales > 0

transaction / traffic growth < 0

ticket / check growth > 0

Label:

Ticket-led growth with demand pressure

Do NOT call it price-led unless source explicitly identifies pricing.

Example operator interpretation:

Topline comp growth is positive while reported customer/transaction volume is declining.

38. Pattern: transaction-led growth

Condition:

comp sales > 0

transaction / traffic growth > 0

transaction contribution appears at least as large as ticket where both available

Label:

Demand-led comp growth

39. Pattern: balanced comp growth

Condition:

comp >0

transactions >0

ticket >0

Label:

Traffic + ticket expansion

40. Pattern: comp decline despite ticket support

Condition:

comp <0

transactions <0

ticket >0

Label:

Traffic decline overwhelms ticket

This is highly relevant to growth-operator intuition.

41. Pattern: digital outperformance

Condition:

digital/eCommerce growth available

comparable or total sales growth available

digital growth exceeds underlying sales growth by material threshold

Default threshold:

+5 percentage points

Label:

Digital channel outperformance

Make threshold configurable.

42. Pattern: unit-expansion-led topline

Condition:

total sales growth materially exceeds comparable sales

net new locations / location growth positive

Label:

Footprint expansion contributing materially to topline

Do not numerically attribute exact share without data.

43. Pattern: loyalty / membership momentum

Condition requires at least one directly reported loyalty metric:

loyalty user/member growth

loyalty sales growth

membership fee growth

renewal growth

Label:

Reported loyalty / membership momentum

No claim of incremental causal value.

